//! Property and invariant tests for `quantum::algorithms`.
//!
//! # Purpose
//!
//! This module verifies invariants shared by the complete quantum-algorithm
//! subsystem without depending on concrete backend implementations.
//!
//! The tests deliberately exercise public contracts rather than private
//! implementation details. This prevents later implementation changes in
//! `error.rs`, `execution.rs`, `optimizer.rs`, VQE, QAOA, Grover, or the other
//! algorithm modules from forcing this file to be rewritten.
//!
//! # Covered contracts
//!
//! - stable algorithm identifiers;
//! - stable algorithm-version ordering;
//! - metadata identity;
//! - explicit deterministic seeds;
//! - typed parameter indices;
//! - positive and bounded qubit counts;
//! - positive and bounded shot counts;
//! - finite probability values;
//! - probability range enforcement;
//! - finite expectation values;
//! - finite objective values;
//! - finite energy values;
//! - rejection of NaN and infinity;
//! - boundary/resource-limit enforcement;
//! - display stability for machine-readable identifiers;
//! - value equality/ordering invariants;
//! - absence of unsafe assumptions.
//!
//! # Integration boundary
//!
//! This file depends only on:
//!
//! ```text
//! quantum::algorithms::error
//! quantum::algorithms::types
//! ```
//!
//! It intentionally does NOT depend directly on:
//!
//! - quantum IR;
//! - circuit implementations;
//! - simulators;
//! - hardware;
//! - routing;
//! - transpilation;
//! - error correction;
//! - optimizer implementations;
//! - concrete algorithm implementations.
//!
//! Those integration paths belong in `integration.rs` and `determinism.rs`.
//!
//! # Dependency contract
//!
//! ```text
//! error.rs
//!    │
//!    ▼
//! types.rs
//!    │
//!    ▼
//! properties.rs
//! ```
//!
//! No production module depends on this test module.
//!
//! # Rust compatibility
//!
//! Rust 1.97.1.
//!
//! No nightly features.
//! No external property-testing crate.
//!
//! The tests use deterministic boundary/value sets instead of a third-party
//! random generator so that the algorithm test suite remains dependency-free
//! and reproducible.
//!
//! # Stability rule
//!
//! Do not match individual `AlgorithmError` fields here. Error representation
//! is owned by `error.rs`; this test file verifies observable acceptance or
//! rejection behavior only. This is intentional and prevents coupling to the
//! internal diagnostic representation.

#![deny(unsafe_code)]
#![deny(unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn)]
#![deny(unused_must_use)]

use super::super::types::{
    AlgorithmId,
    AlgorithmMetadata,
    AlgorithmVersion,
    Energy,
    ExpectationValue,
    ParameterIndex,
    Probability,
    QubitCount,
    Seed,
    ShotCount,
    DEFAULT_MAX_QUBITS,
    DEFAULT_MAX_SHOTS,
